---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SplitTheGGame from '../../../components/SplitTheGGame.astro';
import { BRAND } from '../../../scripts/split-the-g/physics';
import { SPLIT_MEDALS } from '../../../data/medals';
const t = SPLIT_MEDALS.thresholds;
---
<Base title="Split the G · CrinkleCutSnV's playground" description="One pint, one gulp: stop drinking with the line right through the middle of the G.">
  <section class="wrap game-page">
    <div class="title-row">
      <h1>Split the G 🍺</h1>
      <a class="back" href="/">← All apps</a>
    </div>
    <SplitTheGGame />
    <details class="how">
      <summary>How it works</summary>
      <p>Inspired by the pub craze. A settled pint of {BRAND}, the black stuff, sits on the bar with a big G printed on the glass. Take one gulp: press and hold anywhere on the pub (or hold Space) to drink, and let go to stop. Get the line where the stout meets the creamy head to finish exactly through the middle of the G, level with its bar. That's a split.</p>
      <p>Just like the real thing, it's one gulp per pint. Once you let go, that's your go. And it isn't over the moment you let go: the glass takes a moment to come back down, so a little more goes down while it does, and then the head settles and gives the line back a millimetre or two. Every drinker sips differently, too, so get to know the regulars.</p>
      <p>The ref judges the glass once it's back on the bar and settled. Medals: gold within {t.gold} mm of a perfect split, silver within {t.silver} mm, bronze within {t.bronze} mm.</p>
      <p class="small">It's a skill game about one pint. Please enjoy real ones responsibly.</p>
    </details>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .game-page { padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .title-row { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.4rem); margin: .25rem 0 1rem; }
  .back { font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .how { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 70ch; line-height: 1.5; }
  .how summary { font-weight: 800; cursor: pointer; }
  .small { font-size: .9rem; opacity: .75; }
</style>
